{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:62f477c833d82cab","name":"Keetael Talent Tree","source":{"id":"source:reference-62f477c833d82cab","title":"Keetael Talent Tree","revision":19203,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T21:31:16Z","sha256":"10d11f998fea80830cd9755343c93b2b14269c0f635149b88bfa15b6a58deb54","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19203","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Keetael%20Talent%20Tree&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-62f477c833d82cab","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Keetael learn to efficiently and secretly manipulate ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," in combat. Because of their long lives, they gain certain advantages when attempting to view the past through ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"},". Only Force-users that are part of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Keetael"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Keetael","referenceId":"reference:92a919539ac266fb"}," may select ",{"tag":"a","children":["Talents"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Talents","referenceId":"reference:e8871b70ebfa07d9"}," from this tree.\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Core Talents"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Conceal Force Use"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["You have learned to use ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," without telltale gestures, reducing the disturbances created in the process. Whenever you make a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use the Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_the_Force","referenceId":"reference:74883d1dd46b87fe"}," check, as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Swift Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swift_Action"}," you can make a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Deception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Deception","referenceId":"reference:17455029fb9994a3"}," check to convey ",{"tag":"a","children":["Deceptive Appearances"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Deceptive_Appearances"}," in order to conceal the effects of your ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use the Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_the_Force","referenceId":"reference:74883d1dd46b87fe"}," use. Normal modifiers for the Deception's complexity still apply.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Force Direction"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["You can use ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," to guide your ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ranged Attacks"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ranged_Attacks","referenceId":"reference:3c89b302f9fd687b"}," to their target. Whenever you spend a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Point"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Point"}," to add to a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ranged Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ranged_Attack"}," roll, you can always add +3 (or +4, if you roll d8s for ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"},") instead of rolling the die.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Force Momentum"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["You use ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," to add to the impact of your melee weapon, increasing your damage. Whenever you spend a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Point"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Point"}," to add to a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Melee Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Melee_Attack"}," roll, if the attack hits you can also add the Force Point's result to the damage roll.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Past Visions"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Prerequisites:"]}," ",{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Visions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Visions"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The long-lived ",{"tag":"a","children":["Draethos"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Draethos","referenceId":"reference:327e9e97a8c09757"}," are particularly adept at searching and understanding the past. When using ",{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Farseeing"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Farseeing","referenceId":"reference:efdb098bc15b650e"}]}," to look into the past, reduce your DC numbers by half. Also, you are able to see everything within 6 squares of your target clearly without spending a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Point"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Point"},".\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
